{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/5/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2094082456/5`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2094082456/5/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内标记像素的颜色，从区域边界的对应颜色缺口处向外发射射线，射线长度等于该区域内同色标记像素的数量。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为black。\n  - 若干由grey线条围成的封闭矩形区域分布在网格上，每个区域的grey边框上有若干单像素缺口，每个缺口处有一个彩色像素（非grey、非black），颜色各异。\n  - 每个区域内部（black底）散布着若干彩色像素点，其颜色恰好属于该区域边框缺口上出现的颜色子集。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个封闭区域，统计其内部每种颜色的像素数量。\n  - 找到边框上该颜色所在的缺口位置，从缺口处向区域外部发射一条射线，方向为缺口的朝外法线方向（缺口在上边框则向上，在下边框则向下，左边框向左，右边框向右）。\n  - 射线长度（像素数）等于区域内该颜色像素的计数值。\n  - 射线用对应颜色绘制，覆盖路径上的black像素；若射线遇到非black像素或网格边界则提前终止。\n  - 区域本身（边框和内部）保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：缺口颜色和内部标记颜色形成配对关系，内部像素的数量转化为外部射线的几何长度——解题者需要先发现颜色配对机制，再发现计数-到-长度的映射规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, eval/271d71e2, train/aa62e3f4, train/6ca952ad, eval/b9e38dc0, train/2b9ef948, train/ac6f9922, eval/3e6067c3\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4553\nmechanism=0.5183\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, operation:draw_line, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4073\nmechanism=0.4754\nlexical=0.0199\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:path, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/271d71e2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/271d71e2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n\nRule:\n- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n\nKey insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"rectangular container with head that has same color as destination line\",\n  \"path\": \"head forward\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach the destination line or move_distance == s.inner_gey_pixels.num\",\n  \"type2\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src2\": \"inner grey pixels whose num == move_distance\",\n  \"transform\": \"change color to orange\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"grey pixels change color in order\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3510\nmechanism=0.3645\nlexical=0.0155\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:draw_line, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/aa62e3f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3805\nmechanism=0.4671\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, output:same_size, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6ca952ad.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6ca952ad.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground objects with area greater than three pixels\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical downward ray in the object's original columns until its bbox bottom touches the grid bottom\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate the whole object once without changing shape or color\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear moved objects at their original positions; leave foreground objects of area at most three pixels fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b9e38dc0\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3820\nmechanism=0.4570\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:path, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b9e38dc0.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b9e38dc0.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).\n- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.\nRule:\n- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.\n- Obstacles cast \"shadows\" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.\n\nKey insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"A pixel inside a half-surrounded area fills and radiates outward along the border opening, while isolated pixels move to grid edge in the radiate direction, leaving background trail\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"innermost connected same-color pixel s inside the half-surrounded inner area of a sprite\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"fill the surrounded area and radiate along the surrounded border opening\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood_fill\",\n    \"ray_casting\",\n    \"path_extension\",\n    \"obstacle\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"In the second transformation, the sprite s acts as an obstacle blocking the path of s2\",\n  \"type2\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src2\": \"isolated color pixel s2 away from the surrounded area bottleneck\",\n  \"dst2\": \"\",\n  \"match_cond2\": \"\",\n  \"path2\": \"straight line to the edge of the grid, same as the radiate direction\",\n  \"trajectory2\": \"bg color\",\n  \"transform2\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2b9ef948\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3502\nmechanism=0.4214\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
